to prevent crimes and to protect the masses.

ch@a

Accenture is responsible for storing, developing and maintaining the data and analytical systems for reduction and prevention of
crimes in Chicago.

Accenture wishes to leverage Python with Data Analysis libraries like Numpy, Pandas and Matplotlib to fulfill the requirements


2. Challenges

. Currently, the CPD has to put in a lot of time and effort in manually performing the analysis of the huge number of crimes which
get reported every day.


. There is no system in place to record and track the crime rates on a real time basis and hence the CPD is not able to contain the
crime rates within the city in a near-real time fashion which is causing a huge damage to the public and society in general.



. The senior most officers of the CPD are not getting a big picture understanding of different types of crime happening in the city
and hence they are not able to come up with preventive measures like having more patrols going around the most vulnerable
crime areas to mitigate the crimes.

3. Business Need

. The requirement is to stage, process and store the crimes data and transform it to the analytical needs. Finally build
reports/visualizations (using Matplotlib and Seaborn ) which provide actionable insights.



. Another requirement is to ingest the crime data to get near real-time recommendations to prevent crimes in the city.



. Additionally, none of the data should be discarded. In fact, it should be preserved for enabling use-cases related to regulatory
compliance, public safety, insurance, prevention and deduction of crimes in the city.



CPD wants Accenture to build a Data Warehousing (MySQL) platform to store all data related to crimes in order to analyze the
data for better visibility on crime trends, to minimize and prevent crimes and to ensure public safety in whole of Chicago.


4. Expectations from the Development Teams

. Considering the Volume, Velocity and Veracity aspects of the data, Accenture has decided to build a Datawarehouse in Mysql.

. Accenture has analyzed various available options and planned to delivered some Proof of Concepts based on the data received
from the CPD with the help of the teams identified for Python Full Stack Program.

. The teams are expected to design and implement a end-to-end Python data pipeline and web application that ingests and
processes crime data, stores it in a MySQL database, performs analytical processing using Pandas and NumPy, generates visual
insights using Matplotlib, and export the reports.

Note: Incase MySQL is not available use SQLite3


